# FREEZE -- the dispatcher allowlist. bin/freeze-check.sh refuses dispatch at
# exit 1 for any account not named EXEMPT below, on every host, regardless of
# what any rotation says.
#
# HOST-SCOPED ON PURPOSE. `EXEMPT: ecosim` would unfreeze ecosim everywhere,
# including hosts where its row exists at enabled=0, so one edit there would
# arm a second host silently. Naming the host means an exemption cannot travel.
#
# A COMMENTED LINE GENUINELY DISARMS. freeze-check matches
# `^[[:space:]]*EXEMPT:`, so a leading `#` is not cosmetic. Commented entries
# below are paused projects, kept visible so a pause is distinguishable from a
# project that was never armed.
#
# THIS FILE IS SLATED FOR SUNSET -- hf7y/scheduler#187. Its decision history
# (why each account was armed, the chezz and crt pauses and their conditions,
# the enforce_admins precondition for realisateur/scheduler) was moved there
# 2026-08-14 rather than carried here, because prose in a file nobody rereads
# is how it went stale in the first place. Read the issue, not a comment block.
#
# WHAT IT IS STILL DOING, as of 2026-08-14: crt, sequestria and secretaire all
# have enabled=1 rows in _paced.monkey.conf, accounts, clones and runner ticks
# -- and no line here. This file is the only thing keeping them dark. Deleting
# it arms three projects the same tick. That is the argument #187 has to answer
# before anything is removed.

